     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 2400 mg four times daily is 9,600 mg/day, about three times the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg. Ibuprofen has no indication that needs that dose. Past the ceiling you get more toxicity (GI hemorrhage, AKI, fluid retention, cardiovascular events) and no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. Normal kidney and liver function don't change that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the range.** For example, 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum). I can enter either one now.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you have a specific reason for a dose above the maximum, a pharmacist or your attending should review it first. It would likely need a documented rationale and a different ordering pathway than I can offer.\n- **Revisit the pain plan.** If 3,200 mg/day isn't enough, adding acetaminophen or another analgesic class is safer than raising the ibuprofen.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
